{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Input Layer.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Input Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"physical input layer physical input layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Input Layer.md","fileName":"Physical Input Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Physical Input Layer","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Mechanics and Rules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Input Device","Game Verb","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Input Layer.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Input Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"physical input layer physical input layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Input Layer.md","fileName":"Physical Input Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Physical Input Layer","heading":"Physical Input Layer","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The physical input layer is the bodily action and [[Input Device|input mechanism]] through which a player performs a [[Game Verb]]. A digital action may be represented onscreen, but the player actually presses, holds, releases, points, swipes, or moves a control.\n\nDifferent inputs provide different degrees and rhythms of control. A binary key suits discrete grid movement, while a mouse supports continuous motion on two axes. The design should use the properties of its input method and make the physical performance reinforce the pace and character of the represented verb.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Mechanics and Rules","Input Device","Game Verb","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Input Layer.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Ful